Comment:
 This file quotes the Developer Certificate of Origin version 1.1 verbatim.

Files: vendor/*
Copyright: The authors of the vendored crates
License: MIT or Apache-2.0
Comment:
 The Rust crates this package depends on are bundled rather than taken from the
 librust-*-dev packages of the archive: they are shipped as vendored sources in
 the vendor component of the upstream tarball and built offline. See
 debian/README.source for why. Each vendored crate keeps its own copyright and
 license files under vendor/<crate>/, which are the authoritative notices.
 .
 The tree covers more than what is linked into the binaries: the build time
 dependencies, the test dependencies and the crates that only apply to another
 platform are vendored as well, and are therefore covered here too. The stanzas
 that follow carve out every crate known not to be offered under the terms of
 the MIT or the Apache-2.0 license.
 .
 A crate appears under vendor/<name>/ when a single version of it is vendored
 and under vendor/<name>-<version>/ when the three lock files of this source
 package disagree on the version, which is why some of the patterns below come
 in two forms.
 .
 This blanket stanza summarises the licensing of the vendored tree; it is not a
 substitute for per-crate stanzas. Before an upload to the Debian archive,
 replace it with the output of `packaging/vendor-licenses.sh -f dep5`, which
 reads the vendored tree itself and lists every directory in it with the authors
 and the license expression the crate declares, and review the result against
 the files in vendor/<crate>/.

Files: vendor/ucs2/*
       vendor/uefi/*
       vendor/uefi-macros/*
       vendor/uefi-raw/*
Copyright: The uefi-rs project developers
License: MPL-2.0
Comment:
 These crates are only linked into the intel-crashlog-efi package, which is not
 built by default.

Files: vendor/uguid/*
Copyright: The uefi-rs project developers
License: MPL-2.0
Comment:
 Unlike the other crates of the uefi-rs project, this one is an unconditional
 dependency of the library, so it is linked into every binary this source
 package builds.

Files: vendor/cbindgen/*
Copyright: The cbindgen developers
License: MPL-2.0
Comment:
 Build dependency of the library, enabled by the ffi feature, which generates the
 C and C++ headers. None of its code is linked into a binary this source package
 builds, but it is part of the vendored tree.

Files: vendor/aho-corasick/*
       vendor/jiff/*
       vendor/jiff-static/*
       vendor/memchr/*
       vendor/memchr-*/*
Copyright: Andrew Gallant
License: Unlicense or MIT

